er><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>; and if a\ncolumn of <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"\\mathbf{X}\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-TeXAtom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D417 TEX-B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-TeXAtom></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">X</mi></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> is the indicator of a\ngroup, the fitted total over that group equals the observed total.</p>","file":"ch34-exponential-families-glm/03-likelihood-equations.html"}